EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Contested_Isle_Ulster_GrainneIngheanUaitear" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Contested Isle - Gráinne inghean Uaitéar"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Contested_Isle_Core_Ext"

    # Gráinne inghean Uaitéar (Chapter Nine: The Province of Ulster, p109): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.

    #t804894483aaa9dc5f5d733 ^"Gráinne inghean Uaitéar" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#tcdf966f3dff3db195bc5f0 ^"Vigil"]
            ^"Age" STRING "60 (apparent age 38)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Boisterous +3, Flirtatious +2, Protective of Ireland +1 Gráinne inghean Uaitéar (GRAWNyuh IN-yun OO-alt-chair) is every bit as boisterous as the other magi at Vigil. She married the handsome Pádraig when they were both young, her familiar is a female red kite named Úna, with which she share her senses, and her talisman is a bow incorporating numerous materials and attuned with several effects. In the spirit of excess, this is actually her second talisman. After growing tired of her first, she ritually broke the sword and cast the shards off the cliffs at Cionn Mhálanna. This excess is also exhibited in her magic as she suffers from the Waster of Vis Flaw (ArM5, page 61), although she isn’t particularly aware of the difficulty."
            ^"Source" STRING "The Contested Isle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 109
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Her role as the covenant’s quartermaster largely ceremonial and simply requires that large expenditures of vis secure her approval when requested, but she also has authority over the covenant vaults and their uncataloged treasures. Like her predecessors, she has not risen to this authority and has little idea of the vaults’ true value.\n\nGráinne knows about the Verditius right to study and work at Vigil and this might give her the leverage she needs to claim one of the Connacht apprentices at the next Tribunal."
    }

}
